---
import PageLayout from "@/layouts/main.astro";
import Header from "@/components/header.astro";
import { HTTP3AvailabilityTest } from "@/components/tests/http3-availability-test.tsx";
---

<PageLayout title="HE CAD Test | Happy Eyeballs Webtester">
  <Header titleLine1="Happy Eyeballs" titleLine2="HTTP/3 Availability Test">
    <p>
      We operate a web server with HTTP/3 (QUIC) enabled. A subset of the test
      domains pointing to this server publish an HTTPS record that includes the
      <code>h3</code> protocol in the <code>alpn</code> parameter. Additionally, certain
      paths on the server respond with an <code>Alt-Svc</code> header advertising
      HTTP/3 availability. The different test scenarios combine these domains and
      paths in various permutations.
    </p>
    <p>
      We randomize domains to prevent caching effects on the browsers side.
      However, the web server is only assigned a single IP address. Clients that
      cache connection information on a per-address basis rather than a
      per-domain basis may therefore produce skewed results in subsequent test
      runs.
    </p>
  </Header>

  <div class="mt-10">
    <HTTP3AvailabilityTest client:load />
  </div>
</PageLayout>
